animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never saw it that way.<br /> <br /> I saw it more along the lines of &quot;this is a beautiful painting of Abraham Lincoln&quot;. If you went to some uncontacted Amazonian Tribes people and tried to tell them that this painting of Lincoln symbolises Freedom they wouldn't understand you at all.<br /> <br /> Show it to any American and they'd know that before you even said it. (Or they'd be able to explain why they disagree, which is just as good). But show them a picture of William Lloyd Garrison and they probably wouldn't know who that is. Unless I just slipped up and displayed my non-Americanness. *shrug*<br /> <br /> <br /> A Sin-Eater creating a new Ceremony is like an artist creating a beautiful painting. A Krewe is like a culture defining standards of beauty. They don't change the facts, a culture that thinks glasses are sexy isn't going to magically make people's vision worse, or somehow change the physics of light. It's still only working in the realm of the subjective, but in a way that's both deeper and larger than an individual artist.<br /> <br /> So a Krewe that says sacrificing black chickens to the Loa leads to a successful Underworld expedition hasn't actually changed the occult physics of black chickens. Instead they've created the entire framework needed to support the Ceremonial sacrifice of that chicken. In much the same way as that culture created an entire framework a woman could use to influence how the world sees her: If she wants to be seen as beautiful, she wears glasses.<br /> <br /> <br /> TL;DR. A Krewe that believes sacrificing black chickens is good luck isn't changing the occult physics of chickens. They're building a force-multiplying lever. The chicken sacrifice still exerts the same force, but the lever multiplies it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Until a Krewe decides that the fact that unsexy glasses are a component of a Ceremony used to curse someone.. then boom, blindness happens ( either spiritual or physical, doesn't matter, being a death of one's senses either way lol) XD.<br /> <br /> And it does change the occult physics of black chickens - for that Krewe or any Sin-Eaters who decide to co-opt the Ceremony for themselves. Just because it doesn't do the same for other splats doesn't mean it doesn't occur period. Force Multiplier or not.. it's still magically affecting the world when it logically shouldn't from a Mage or other occult scholar's perspective - almost a warping of reality a bit. So you are right, but not entirely right, least that's how I see it- and it's an equally valid viewpoint to yours- both of our views are &quot;right&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> You seem to have missed my Ork comparison, but that's okay lol. Orks are a good way to explain how the Bound's trash-bag magic works even though it really shouldn't though xD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 06-03-2016, 09:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T18:10:08-07:00","id":906857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/888551-sin-eaters-vs-moros-mages?p=905199#post905199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mage storyteller's guide should really go into things that Mages might do in the Underworld or Shadow that will get the local splat angry at them and make that sweet drama.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah we get a franchise of supernatural shadow war films that get progressively bad as they go on <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T18:14:04-07:00","id":906860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/888551-sin-eaters-vs-moros-mages?p=904785#post904785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Underworld is Mount Everest, the Moros are the sponsored, rich, Western climbers who've trained for decades have thousands of dollars of equipment, anti-altitude medication, and are doing it for the experience.<br /> <br /> The Bound are the Sherpas. They're not as well equipped, but they live there, and will still live there after the westerners have fucked off back to their comfortable lives telling stories of their awesome experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we are using the Mount Everest analogy, is it also fair to say that the Mages die in droves in comparison to the native peoples, the sherpas who die regularly, but less often due to not being stupid?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T07:32:32-07:00","id":910770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/888551-sin-eaters-vs-moros-mages?p=906860#post906860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we are using the Mount Everest analogy, is it also fair to say that the Mages die in droves in comparison to the native peoples, the sherpas who die regularly, but less often due to not being stupid?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say if the Sin-Eaters do die less often than mages upon encountering Underworld-related phenomena, it has less to do with them being smarter and/or more savvy, and more to do with how insanely survivable they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T08:15:42-07:00","id":910805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/888551-sin-eaters-vs-moros-mages?p=910770#post910770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say if the Sin-Eaters do die less often than mages upon encountering Underworld-related phenomena, it has less to do with them being smarter and/or more savvy, and more to do with how insanely survivable they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus, they have a partner with them at all times who could arguably be considered something of an expert. And means to interact with Twilight innate via Reverse Possession.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T08:48:03-07:00","id":910838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/888551-sin-eaters-vs-moros-mages?p=910805#post910805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, they have a partner with them at all times who could arguably be considered something of an expert. And means to interact with Twilight innate via Reverse Possession.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the new Attainment system, interacting with Twilight is about as easy for a Death-focused mage as reverse possession is for a Sin-Eater, so I'd no longer count that as an advantage.<br /> <br /> Having a &quot;native guide&quot; with you at all times is certainly a boon, but it's not like a Moros can't consult multiple Underworld denizens on any matter of import. Which may be even better, because a Sin-Eater is somewhat inclined to trust her Geist over other possible sources of information, while a mage is usually inclined to not trust supernatural beings, and cross-checking your info is never a bad idea in the hostile territory.<br /> <br /> Seriously, this Mt Everest analogy works in that it signifies a degree of removal that mages experience compared to Sin-Eaters, but I wouldn't extrapolate it onto any statements about the relative competence of either party or some inherent superiority of one group's approach over the other's, because that's where the analogy starts falling apart. At the end of the day, both can climb the mountain and either can die in the process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T14:39:35-07:00","id":911154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/888551-sin-eaters-vs-moros-mages?p=910838#post910838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the new Attainment system, interacting with Twilight is about as easy for a Death-focused mage as reverse possession is for a Sin-Eater, so I'd no longer count that as an advantage.<br /> <br /> Having a &amp;quot;native guide&amp;quot; with you at all times is certainly a boon, but it's not like a Moros can't consult multiple Underworld denizens on any matter of import. Which may be even better, because a Sin-Eater is somewhat inclined to trust her Geist over other possible sources of information, while a mage is usually inclined to not trust supernatural beings, and cross-checking your info is never a bad idea in the hostile territory.<br /> <br /> Seriously, this Mt Everest analogy works in that it signifies a degree of removal that mages experience compared to Sin-Eaters, but I wouldn't extrapolate it onto any statements about the relative competence of either party or some inherent superiority of one group's approach over the other's, because that's where the analogy starts falling apart. At the end of the day, both can climb the mountain and either can die in the process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps, and in some cases that is absolutely true. But on average, I still believe the typical Moros is far less equipped than the typical Sin-Eater when it comes with dealing with the Underworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}